    "boundary": "The shared Lazard operator exposes final coprime factor item identities separately from complete provenance. CAC and global Lazard lifting isolate those active factors; original products and all parent links remain available for proof replay. All lower projection polynomials and original atom truth are preserved. Three previous implementations are recompiled against identical fixed ABI headers and must fail all3 new active-factor contracts; corrected sources are restored before rebuilding every native target. Exact interval tests cover nullification, factor overlap and leading-degree drops. Full native/Python tests qualify the freeze; original-input model replay and fair public-suite results remain separate. Both protected sets remain unread/unused, with no overall SMT or new original-C QCP superiority claim."
  },
